1. Nested if
= Nested if is useful when a second condition should only be checked after
  the first condition has already been satisfied.


Example;
age = 20
has_id = True

if age >= 18:
if has-id:
print("Entry Allowed")
else:
print("ID Required")
else:
print("Minor")

Output:
Entry Allowed


